From 0ca0a4650b53b8dcb2b54fbeddd999248062590d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ares libretro <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:53:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a libretro core (ares_libretro)

Adds libretro/, a frontend that exposes ares as a libretro core. It loads
content and firmware through mia, boots the ares node tree, and implements
ares::Platform on top of the libretro API (video, audio, input, paks), with
save states, core options, per-port peripheral selection, rumble and FDS
disk control. Controller layouts are generated from desktop-ui's own
definitions by libretro/tools/gen-input-map.py.

Supporting changes:
- CMake: ARES_BUILD_DESKTOP (default ON) and ARES_BUILD_LIBRETRO (default
  OFF). With defaults the desktop build is unchanged.
- ares: ARES_VIDEO_UNTHREADED renders frames synchronously so they arrive
  inside retro_run(); defined only for libretro builds.
- mia: setResourceLocation() hook so a frontend can say where Database/ is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011EepHr27X2UYRekCuNmGCX
