From b3567637ee745b13ab8b4f40f6ca1e22b8f9cfec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ares libretro <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:19:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] libretro: Windows build support, CI, and licensing

- .github/workflows/libretro.yml builds ares_libretro on Windows (Visual
  Studio + ClangCL, the toolchain used for official ares releases; plus a
  best-effort MSYS2/MinGW job) and Linux, runs the smoke tests against the
  built core, and uploads installable packages.
- The test harness loads cores with LoadLibrary on Windows, can assert
  pixel values, and is built by CMake with -DARES_LIBRETRO_TESTS=ON;
  tests/run.sh is shared by CI and local runs.
- Fix a MinGW link-option generator expression that CMake would have split
  in two.
- Licensing: libretro/ is ISC like ares (SPDX headers, LICENSE);
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt covers bundled components not in ares' LICENSE
  (zstd, miniz, paraLLEl-RDP, libretro.h). cmake --install ships the
  license files with the binary, and no longer installs the import library.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011EepHr27X2UYRekCuNmGCX
