+### Windows (`ares_libretro.dll`)
+
+ares chooses its platform configuration from the *host* operating system, so Windows
+binaries are built on Windows (as the official ares releases are); cross-compiling from Linux
+is not supported by ares' build system.
+
+**GitHub Actions (easiest):** push this tree to a GitHub fork of ares. The `libretro`
+workflow (`.github/workflows/libretro.yml`) builds the core with Visual Studio + ClangCL,
+runs the smoke tests against the DLL, and uploads `ares_libretro-windows-x64` (cores/,
+info/, system/ares/Database/, licenses/) as a workflow artifact. Linux and an MSYS2/MinGW
+variant are built too. You can also start it by hand from the Actions tab.
+
+**Visual Studio 2026** (with the "C++ Clang tools for Windows" component), from Git Bash or
+a developer prompt in the ares source directory:
+
+```sh
+cmake --preset windows-ci-cl-native -DARES_BUILD_LIBRETRO=ON -DARES_BUILD_DESKTOP=OFF -DARES_BUILD_OPTIONAL_TARGETS=OFF
+cmake --build build --config RelWithDebInfo --target ares_libretro
+# result: build/libretro/RelWithDebInfo/ares_libretro.dll
+```
+
+The preset links the C runtime statically, so the DLL needs no Visual C++ redistributable.
+
+**MSYS2** (CLANG64 shell, packages `mingw-w64-clang-x86_64-toolchain`, `-cmake`, `-ninja`):
+
+```sh
+cmake --preset windows-ci-mingw-native -DARES_BUILD_LIBRETRO=ON -DARES_BUILD_DESKTOP=OFF -DARES_BUILD_OPTIONAL_TARGETS=OFF
+cmake --build build --target ares_libretro
+# result: build/libretro/ares_libretro.dll
+```
+
 Building the libretro core turns on position-independent code for all of ares and defines
